@title Rooftop Solar Bid Comparison
@subtitle Ridgeway School District, six schools. For Beatrice Ng, facilities director. Board vote on 2026-11-17

# Bids

table = Bidder,Size (kW),Price,25-year savings,Warranty (years); SunHarvest,1200,"$2,640,000","$7,400,000",25; Brightline Energy,1150,"$2,415,000","$7,050,000",20; Copperfield Solar,1250,"$2,875,000","$7,900,000",25; Halcyon Power,1100,"$2,640,000","$6,800,000",30; Meridian Renewables,1200,"$2,400,000","$7,150,000",15

# Net benefit

Net 25-year benefit is savings minus price.

data net = bidder,net; Copperfield Solar,5025000; SunHarvest,4760000; Meridian Renewables,4750000; Brightline Energy,4635000; Halcyon Power,4160000

chart hbar net unit=$ labels title="Net 25-year benefit, highest first"

# Schedule fit

Panels must be generating before the school year starts on 2027-09-01.

table = Bidder,Complete by,Done before 2027-09-01; Copperfield Solar,2027-07-31,Yes; SunHarvest,2027-08-15,Yes; Meridian Renewables,2027-08-31,Yes; Brightline Energy,2027-09-30,No; Halcyon Power,2027-10-31,No

Brightline and Halcyon would finish after the school year starts.

# Recommendation

We recommend Copperfield Solar. It has the highest net benefit, $265,000 above SunHarvest, and the earliest completion, on 2027-07-31. It also has the highest upfront price, $2,875,000, which the district must finance.
